# Generation speed backlog (Anthony: Generate → preview too slow)

Phase 1.5 mobile verify is complete enough to start this work. Prefer **same API $**; do not thin prompts or drop retries.

## Status

1. **Parallel hydrate** — **DONE** (bounded concurrency 3 for `hydrateCourseContent` chunks in [`src/services/aiService.ts`](src/services/aiService.ts); Tier 1→2→3 + Bug #7 safety net kept).
2. **Image pacing** — **DONE** (concurrency 2 + ~400ms pace in [`src/services/imageService.ts`](src/services/imageService.ts); was 1.2–2.0s fully sequential; 429 single retry kept).
3. **Perceived speed** — **NEXT** — open preview after hydrate (+ cover); continue content images / AI QC async, or defer AI QC past first preview ([`src/App.tsx`](src/App.tsx) `finalizeGeneratedCourse`, [`src/services/qcService.ts`](src/services/qcService.ts)).

## Explicitly deprioritize first

- Throwing money at larger/faster models for every slide (higher cost, unclear wall-clock win).
- Thinning prompts / dropping retries in ways that raise blank-slide risk.

## Context

- Wall clock was dominated by sequential Haiku hydrate + paced images + QC/exam before preview; TTS is already after preview.
- Backend note: full hydrate can be 40–80+ `/api/ai` calls ([`server.js`](server.js)).
- Ship generation-speed changes to **`main` / nexcourse.ai** for pilot impact (not only the Capacitor branch).
